    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2620": {
      "title": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Campus Advocacy, Prevention, and Student Support Specialist",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Campus Advocacy, Prevention, and Student Support Specialist Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Campus Advocacy, Prevention, and Student Support Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Campus Advocacy, Prevention, and Student Support Specialist Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Community & Government Relations Department Office of Campus Advocacy, Prevention, and Education Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary If you are a dedicated advocate ready to lead critical initiatives that protect and empower a university community, this is your next career move! The Specialist of Campus Advocacy, Prevention, and Student Support will serve multiple functions within the university community, primarily leading the university’s prevention, education, response to, and reporting of issues related to sexual misconduct, interpersonal violence, and stalking. The position will also support the CGR Division’s mission in a generalist capacity by collaborating with university and community partners to promote student, faculty, and staff well-being, safety, and sense of community through outreach and education. Essential Responsibilities: Manage and adjust as needed the (Campus Advocacy, Prevention, and Education) CAPE Project Strategic Plan Hire, manage, and train a peer educator team to assist in peer training on preventing interpersonal violence Gather and develop data collection for university use and related activities, including training and programmatic outcome and attendance data, expense reporting data, and assessment data Oversee and coordinate meetings for the coordinated community response team, provide direction and oversight as needed to various subcommittees Assist students in navigating university resources, providing support and referrals related to academic, personal, and wellness concerns. Support the division’s programmatic efforts View full job description Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Following USCIS regulations, successful applicants must be legally able to accept work in the United States. Doane is unable to sponsor applicants for work visas. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary $51,500 Minimum Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree plus one (1) year of experience in program development, implementation, and evaluation of program effectiveness and strategies. Experience must demonstrate: Expertise in topics of interpersonal violence prevention and advocacy in a higher education or social service setting Skills in crisis management and the ability to navigate complex relationships with extensive knowledge of confidentiality and relevant laws are required. Ability to conduct educational programs and training workshops Familiarity with promising practices related to policy development and survivor advocacy, knowledge of laws, regulations, guidance, including Title IX, VAWA /Campus SAVE , and Clery Strong organizational skills Capacity to work effectively with teams and interpersonal skills to work effectively with a diverse population of constituents Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in higher education, counseling, counselor education, psychology, social work, public health, or a related field preferred Required Licenses/Certifications Eligible to become and maintain designation as a Designated School Official ( DSO ) with the U.S. Department of Homeland Security in order to support international students Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Primarily will work during business hours, but some work during evenings and weekends as needed, based on program needs Travel Required No Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF180 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2596 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2740": {
      "title": "Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Work-Study Peer Advisor Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Work-Study Peer Advisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must be eligible for and awarded Federal Work-Study for the 2026-2027 academic year. The Financial Aid Office will verify Federal Work-Study eligibility prior to hire. Position Details Position Information Position Title Work-Study Peer Advisor Department Financial Aid Office Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Supervisor Purpose of Job The role of this position is to provide quality client service to students and families regarding scholarship and financial aid at Doane University. General Description and Duties The duties and responsibilities of this position include, but are not limited to: Answer inquiries by email, phone, and at the FA front desk regarding Doane scholarships and financial aid information. Represent FA at browsing sessions during recruitment events for prospective students. Learn general dates (deadlines) – Scholarships Deadlines, FAFSA Priority Date, Term Dates, and general timelines for aid processes. Serve as the reception person at the front counter and on phones. Learn priority dates for the Doane scholarship application, FAFSA , academic term beginning and ending dates, and timeline for scholarship and financial aid process. One-on-one counseling, in person and over the phone, to assist students and parents in the completion of the FAFSA , office forms, and applications, U.S. Department of Education procedures, and forms. Provide information about financial aid requirements and policies, and refer students and parents to office staff as appropriate. Assist in the processing of financial aid files and forms. Special Skills or Knowledge Required Applicants must be eligible for and awarded Federal Work-Study for the 2026-2027 academic year. The Financial Aid Office will verify Federal Work-Study eligibility prior to hire. High ability to work with the public daily (students, parents, future students). Must be able to maintain a high degree of confidentiality regarding all work. Strong attention to detail is critical. Need a high level of problem-solving skills. Total Weekly Hours Required Flexible, $15.00/hour Physical Demands Posting Detail Information Posting Number STU129 Number of Vacancies Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Review Start Date 03/06/2026 Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants must be eligible for and awarded Federal Work-Study for the 2026-2027 academic year. The Financial Aid Office will verify Federal Work-Study eligibility prior to hire. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2322 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current Doane University student? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2686": {
      "title": "Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Athletics Development Officer Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Athletics Development Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Athletics Development Officer Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Institutional Advancement Department Development Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Elevate your passion for collegiate sports into a rewarding fundraising career at Doane University as our Athletics Development Officer. In this role, you have the opportunity to support the Advancement and Athletics offices in achieving their annual fundraising goals across all giving levels. This position provides hands-on experience in athletics donor relations, annual giving, event coordination, corporate sponsorships, and major gift support. If you are a motivated self-starter with a passion for collegiate athletics, this is your chance to build a career in advancement and fundraising. View full job description Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary $57,000 - $60,000 Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a bachelor’s degree in Sports Management, Communications, Business, Marketing, or a related field. Success in the role requires: Strong written and verbal communication skills Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint) Demonstrated enthusiasm for collegiate athletics Preferred Qualifications We would also like to see: Prior internship or experience in fundraising, development, sales, or athletics administration Familiarity with CRM platforms (e.g., Salesforce) Experience with event planning or volunteer coordination Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Willingness to work evenings, weekends, and home athletic events as required Travel Required Yes Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Exposed to both indoor and outdoor elements Background Check Required Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF194 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2685 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
