    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2744": {
      "title": "Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Online Adjunct Faculty - School of Natural and Life Sciences and Open Learning Academy. Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Online Adjunct Faculty - School of Natural and Life Sciences and Open Learning Academy. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and transcripts (unofficial transcripts accepted for the application). Due to this being an ongoing job advertisement, only applicants selected for interviews will be contacted; turn-down notices will not be provided. Position Details Position Information Position Title Online Adjunct Faculty - School of Natural and Life Sciences and Open Learning Academy. Unit Extended Learning Opportunities Job Location Remote/Hybrid Option Description of Work Doane University, a nationally recognized liberal arts and sciences university in Nebraska, invites applications for an Online Adjunct Faculty position for the School of Natural and Life Sciences and Open Learning Academy. Doane University’s Open Learning Academy is seeking adjunct faculty for the following course topics: Organic Chemistry I and II and Biochemistry. The Open Learning Academy offers rigorous 5-, 8-, and 16-week courses online to students across the nation. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications Masters degree Official transcripts will be required at the time of hire as a condition of employment. Preferred Qualifications Terminal degree Priority will be given to candidates with online teaching experience. Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required No Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC066 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and transcripts (unofficial transcripts accepted for the application). Due to this being an ongoing job advertisement, only applicants selected for interviews will be contacted; turn-down notices will not be provided. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2743 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
