    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2708": {
      "title": "Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Digital Resource Librarian Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Digital Resource Librarian Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Digital Resource Librarian Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Technology Services Department Learning Technology and Library Services Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary The Digital Resources Librarian is a forward-thinking professional responsible for managing and implementing new technology and digital resources to enhance library services and user experiences. This role is designed to grow with a successful candidate, and early-career librarians are encouraged to apply! This role involves hands-on work with emerging technology, digital tools, and resources. This librarian is also expected to work collaboratively with teaching faculty and staff to support innovative learning, teaching, and research at the institution. Reporting to the Director of Learning Technology and Library Services, the Digital Resources Librarian works closely with library staff, faculty, instructional developers, and IT teams to ensure library systems and resources meet the evolving needs of students and academic programs. The Digital Resources Librarian plays a critical role in advancing the library’s mission to provide accessible, innovative, and high-quality services that support the institution’s academic and research needs. View full job description Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary Salary range: $53,600 - $58,000 Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a Master’s degree in Library and Information Science ( MLIS ) or equivalent from an ALA -accredited program plus two years of experience with library technology systems, such as ILS , discovery platforms, and digital repositories. Experience should demonstrate Practical understanding of metadata standards and practices (e.g., MARC , Dublin Core, or other metadata schemas). Excellent problem-solving skills and the ability to troubleshoot technical issues effectively. Strong project management skills with the ability to handle multiple priorities and deadlines. Excellent communication and collaboration skills to work effectively with diverse stakeholders. Commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in library services and technology initiatives. Preferred Qualifications Certification or training in relevant technologies, systems, or programming languages is a plus. Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required No Physical Requirements Light work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF197 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2707 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
