    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2753": {
      "title": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Grounds and Landscape Associate",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Grounds and Landscape Associate Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Grounds and Landscape Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Grounds and Landscape Associate Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Finance and Administration Department Grounds & Fleet Services Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Doane University in Crete, Nebraska, is hiring a Grounds and Landscape Associate. This position involves working with duties related to groundskeeping and landscape maintenance. This includes: lawn and grounds care, maintenance of lawn equipment and vehicles, as well as snow removal. This position may require work assignments at times other than regular scheduled shifts. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Hourly (Non-exempt) Salary $16.50 per hour Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a high school diploma or equivalent and a year of experience working in grounds or maintenance and repair in one or more of the craft disciplines. Knowledge of methods, practices, tools, and all other equipment and materials utilized in general grounds and landscape maintenance. Knowledge of safety hazards and appropriate precautionary methods involved in grounds and landscape maintenance. Ability to operate trucks and tractor equipment. Skilled in the safe use of tools and equipment utilized in grounds and landscape maintenance. Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing with the general public and a diverse staff and student population. Ability to maintain and repair lawn care and snow removal equipment and all other tools as needed. Preferred Qualifications Required Licenses/Certifications Valid Nebraska driver’s License and driving record acceptable to the University’s automobile insurance provider. Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Working outdoors in extreme temperatures, with occasional weekend shifts during peak seasons such as homecoming and graduation. Travel Required No Physical Requirements Medium work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to outdoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF203 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2752 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
