    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2710": {
      "title": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further inquiries on the position, please email Sara Simonsen, Operations Manager of the College of Business, Humanities, and Technology, sara.simonsen@doane.edu . Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcript of graduate degrees or graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing Unit College of Business Job Location Crete, NE & Lincoln, NE Description of Work The School of Business and Leadership ( SBL ) at Doane University is seeking applicants for a full-time tenure-track faculty position as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Marketing. The SBL at Doane University is ACBSP -accredited and serves both undergraduate and graduate students at campuses located in Crete and Lincoln, Nebraska. The SBL provides a highly collaborative and collegial environment that is very supportive of teaching, scholarship activities, and faculty development. Responsibilities will include teaching a total of up to 24 credit hours per academic year across a variety of marketing courses. Course modality could include both online and in-person sections. Course location could include both Crete residential campus and Lincoln non-residential campus, teaching both undergraduate and graduate students. We have a strong interest in faculty with expertise in one or more areas, including digital marketing, marketing research, and marketing strategy. The anticipated start date for the position is August 2027. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the university. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. or DBA in Marketing earned or in progress Academically qualified to meet ACBSP accreditation standards Successful experience as an instructor in marketing Commitment to ongoing professional activity and scholarship Candidates must have knowledge of methods to effectively instruct, motivate, and evaluate both undergraduate and graduate students, as well as: Teach across a variety of modalities Engage in faculty scholarly and service activities Participate in continuous improvement efforts within the SBL Preferred Qualifications Relevant industry experience Undergraduate, graduate, face-to-face, and online teaching experience Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel between Doane campuses in Crete and Lincoln Travel Required Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC060 Desired Start Date 08/09/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further inquiries on the position, please email Sara Simonsen, Operations Manager of the College of Business, Humanities, and Technology, sara.simonsen@doane.edu . Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcript of graduate degrees or graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2644 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2712": {
      "title": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant Professor of Engineering",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant Professor of Engineering Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Assistant Professor of Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin on October 12th, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial transcripts accepted for applications). Official transcripts of degree or degree in progress will be required as a condition for employment. For further inquiries on the position, please email academicaffairs@doane.edu Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Engineering Unit Engineering & Physics Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Description of Work Doane University, a liberal arts university with campuses in Crete and Lincoln and an Omaha Location, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Engineering with an anticipated start date of August 2027. The selected candidate will join the growing Engineering & Physics department, which offers an ABET -accredited Bachelor’s degree program in Engineering with specializations in mechanical, civil, electrical, and integrated engineering. Anticipated responsibilities include teaching 24 credit hours per year, supervising engineering design projects, engaging undergraduate students in research, advising majors, and participating actively in the life of the department and university. Open to all engineering disciplines, although preference will be given to mechanical, civil, electrical, or interdisciplinary engineering candidates that would complement the expertise and talent pool of the current faculty. The ideal candidate will be able to teach core engineering courses required of all engineering majors, physics courses, and emphasis area courses within the candidate’s discipline. Candidates with demonstrated teaching and industry experience are particularly encouraged to apply. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications PhD preferred, but ABD or professional licensure will be considered for appointment as Visiting Assistant Professor or Assistant Professor of Practice At least one degree (undergraduate or graduate) in engineering from an ABET -accredited program Experience working in interdisciplinary engineering environments and engaging in fundamental engineering learning experiences Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates who have experience in an active learning and teaching environment, value interdisciplinary studies, are committed to teaching a diverse population of students, including students with different perspectives, and are responsive to student needs. Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required No Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC064 Desired Start Date 08/09/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date 10/12/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Review of applications will begin on October 12th, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial transcripts accepted for applications). Official transcripts of degree or degree in progress will be required as a condition for employment. For further inquiries on the position, please email academicaffairs@doane.edu Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2700 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
