    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2714": {
      "title": "Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Senior Creative Manager Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Senior Creative Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Senior Creative Manager Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Enrollment Management Department Office of Strategic Marketing Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Doane University is hiring a Senior Creative Manager who is an integral part of the Office of Strategic Marketing ( OSM ). The position reports to the Director of Marketing and manages Doane’s overall brand, ensuring consistency and accuracy across all media/outlets. Primarily, this position will develop and maintain the Doane brand, develop video creative, participate in strategic planning, and design and develop marketing and advertising collateral pieces based on established brand and design standards and desired objectives. In addition, this position approves/guides the design process of externally created materials. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary $52,221 - $57,222 Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a bachelor’s degree plus three years of progressively responsible design experience in: Creating marketing/advertising campaigns — from developing the vision and messaging platform to overseeing production on time and within budget Creating integrated content across all marketing channels: digital, social media, paid media, mobile, offline, and print Developing successful concepts Working with Adobe Creative Suite programs Digital asset management software Experience must demonstrate: Comprehensive knowledge of paper, inks, prepress processes (including bleeds, separations, PDFs, etc.), and understanding of print production (monotone to four-color printing, spot colors, coatings, etc.). Comprehensive knowledge of designing for digital mediums (websites, applications, emails, etc.) and associated processes ( RGB vs. CMYK , resolution, aspect ratios, etc.). Support video creative to include storyboard, preproduction, video editing, and post-production. Spearhead and manage content strategy for projects, harnessing brand design, copy, art and digital technology. High proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite apps, Microsoft products and other design tools. Proficient in both Mac and Windows environments. Superior communication and leadership skills. Excellent ability to establish and maintain good working relationships with colleagues and vendors. Strong organizational skills and the ability to work effectively under pressure, handling multiple projects and tight deadlines. Strengths in creative typography, corporate branding and application of branding/visual standards. High energy, self-motivated with a strong work ethic. Strong attention to detail. Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to work within a team environment. Collaborate with the team in developing marketing creative, analyzing results, and identifying opportunities. Expertise in developing marketing creative that translate objectives across business units into clear and motivating creative strategies Skilled at prioritizing work and resources across engagements, based on short- and long-term needs, and developing schedules by collaborating with the OSM team. Ability to review and approve art and copy developed by the team, ensuring that deliverables address marketing goals and challenges effectively. Skilled at producing fresh, innovative work that translates complex ideas into compelling print materials and digital experiences for audiences. Preferred Qualifications A master’s degree is preferred as well as: Experience leading other designers/students Experience as a copywriter, graphic designer or production artist Experience in project management, with a focus on creative direction Experience in video creative Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Availability outside of typical work hours due to University events is required. Travel Required No Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF190 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2666 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Portfolio Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
