    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2722": {
      "title": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant Professor of History",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant Professor of History Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Assistant Professor of History Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin on October 15, and the search will continue until the position is filled. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcripts of graduate degrees or a graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of History Unit History Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Description of Work Doane University, a nationally recognized liberal arts and sciences university in Crete, Nebraska, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of History starting in the 2027-2028 academic year. This position begins August 16, 2027. Responsibilities include teaching 12 credit hours of on-ground undergraduate courses each semester. The position may also teach select courses online, subject to the needs of the institution. The department is seeking a generalist with the ability to teach World and European history courses. The area of specialization is open. This position will be responsible for introductory courses in world history and advanced courses with a focus on topics such as the history of the ancient world, military history, and country-specific, regional, or broader world history. Candidates may develop courses in their area of expertise as well. The opportunity to teach the program’s gateway and capstone courses, Introduction to Historical Methods and the Writing and Research Seminar, is also possible. During the Fall semester, the position has the opportunity to develop a course in Doane’s LAR 101 First Year Seminar program, with the topic to be chosen by the faculty member. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications Qualifications: Ph.D. or Advanced ABD in History. A commitment to teaching in an undergraduate liberal arts university is expected among strong candidates. A commitment to engage in scholarly and service activities, including academic advising, is expected among strong candidates as well. Preferred Qualifications A background in Museum or Archival Studies is desirable. Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required No Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC065 Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date 10/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Review of applications will begin on October 15, and the search will continue until the position is filled. Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcripts of graduate degrees or a graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2720 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/1862": {
      "title": "Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Adjunct Faculty - College of Business Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Adjunct Faculty - College of Business Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Note - Due to this being an ongoing job advertisement, only applicants selected for interviews will be contacted; turn-down notices will not be provided. Position Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Faculty - College of Business Unit College of Business Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Description of Work Doane University, a nationally recognized liberal arts and sciences university in Nebraska, invites applications for Adjunct Faculty in the College of Business . The newly-formed College of Business offers undergraduate programs in the following areas: Accounting, Agribusiness, Business Administration, Economics, and Leadership. We offer minors in each of these areas, as well as in Finance, Human Resource Management, Management, and Marketing. At the graduate level, we offer an MBA and a Master of Arts in Leadership. The College of Business offers classes in Crete, Lincoln, and online. Our residential campus is located in Crete, with classes offered during the day in 16-week semesters. Most students in Crete are recent high school graduates. The Lincoln campus is geared toward working adults, with classes offered one night a week in the evening during 8-week terms. Most classes meet in person, but a few meet via distance learning. We also offer asynchronous, online classes during the 8-week terms. Candidates will only be considered for academic areas that they are qualified to teach according to our accrediting bodies. For further inquiries on the position, please email daniel.bothe@doane.edu Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the university. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. In accordance with USCIS regulations, successful applicants must be legally able to accept work in the United States. Doane is unable to sponsor applicants for work visas. HOW TO APPLY : If you are interested in teaching a class offered through the College of Business, Click on “Apply for this Job.\" You will then either create an application or edit your current application that is on file. You will be required to attach a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, and one PDF of transcripts of all graduate work in MS Word or PDF format. In your cover letter, clearly state which academic areas you are interested in teaching, as well as which locations (Crete, Lincoln) and modalities (in-person, distance learning, and online) you are willing to teach. Official transcript of terminal degree or degree in progress will be required as a condition for employment. Minimum Required Qualifications A master’s degree is required. Priority will be given to candidates with teaching experience and professional business experience. Preferred Qualifications A terminal degree is preferred. Preference will be given to candidates who have experience in an active learning and teaching environment, value interdisciplinary studies, are committed to teaching to a diverse population of students, include students with different perspectives, and are responsive to student needs. Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC011 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Note – Due to this being an ongoing job advertisement, only applicants selected for interviews will be contacted; turn-down notices will not be provided. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/1161 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2725": {
      "title": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Graduate Assistant - Strength &amp; Conditioning",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Graduate Assistant - Strength &amp; Conditioning Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Graduate Assistant - Strength & Conditioning Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Assistant - Strength & Conditioning Job Type Part Time Division Athletics Department Strength & Conditioning Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Doane University , a nationally recognized liberal arts and sciences university in Crete, NE, invites applications for the position of Graduate Assistant – Strength and Conditioning . We are looking for a coach who understands that they are continually on display and consistently projects positive coaching behavior. As the Graduate Assistant – Strength and Conditioning , you will have the responsibility of working with the Head Coach to manage the sport and student-athletes in the best interest of Doane University and in accordance with all the rules of the NAIA and the GPAC Conference. This position is responsible for student-athlete recruitment and retention and is an integral part of the Doane University Wrestling coaching staff. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the university. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. In accordance with USCIS regulations, successful applicants must be legally able to accept work in the United States. Doane is unable to sponsor applicants for work visas. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary An annual $6,750 stipend is provided, reduced to $5,000 if you live on campus, which includes a single bedroom in Frees Hall and a commuter meal plan of five meals per week plus $200 Doane Dollars per semester. Minimum Required Qualifications Preferred Qualifications Required Licenses/Certifications Valid driver’s license and driving record acceptable to the college’s automobile insurance provider. Ability to obtain certification to drive a Doane full-size minivan once hired. Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Hours outside of standard office hours Travel Required Yes Physical Requirements Medium work Outdoor Exposure Exposed to both indoor and outdoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF199 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2724 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2532": {
      "title": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Graduate Assistant - Women&#39;s Soccer",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Graduate Assistant - Women&#39;s Soccer Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Graduate Assistant - Women's Soccer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The position includes a tuition waiver of up to $5,250 per calendar year (books/fees not included) Medical, dental, and vision insurance plans are available. Position Details Position Information Position Title Graduate Assistant - Women's Soccer Job Type Part Time Division Athletics Department Soccer Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Are you passionate about soccer and ready to start your coaching career? As a Women’s Soccer Graduate Assistant Coach, you’ll have the opportunity to work closely with student-athletes, assist in practice planning and skill development, and gain valuable experience in a competitive collegiate environment. If you’re looking to enhance your coaching skills while earning your graduate degree, this role offers the ideal balance of hands-on experience and academic growth! The Graduate Assistant Coach is responsible for working alongside the Head Coach to manage the women’s soccer program and the student-athletes in the best interest of Doane University and in accordance with all the rules of the NAIA and the GPAC Conference. This position starts August 3, 2026 Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the university. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. In accordance with USCIS regulations, successful applicants must be legally able to accept work in the United States. Doane is unable to sponsor applicants for work visas. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary An annual $6,750 stipend is provided, reduced to $5,000 if you live on campus, which includes a single bedroom in Frees Hall and a commuter meal plan of five meals per week plus $200 Doane Dollars per semester. Minimum Required Qualifications Must qualify for acceptance into a Doane graduate program . Bachelor’s degree with competition or coaching experience at the collegiate level. General knowledge of sport, including rules, techniques, and strategies. The ability to diligently and effectively recruit and retain student-athletes Ability to teach and develop student-athletes Character Requirements: Proven record of integrity, high principles, and demonstrated skill in developing and motivating student-athletes academically and athletically. Must recognize that they are always a representative of the program and must consistently demonstrate positive coaching behavior. Organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Required Licenses/Certifications Valid driver’s license and driving record acceptable to the college’s automobile insurance provider and ability to obtain certification to drive a Doane full-size minivan once hired. Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Willingness to work evenings, weekends, and travel as required. Travel Required Yes Physical Requirements Light work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to outdoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF163 Desired Start Date 08/03/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date 03/02/2026 Review Start Date 03/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant The position includes a tuition waiver of up to $5,250 per calendar year (books/fees not included) Medical, dental, and vision insurance plans are available. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2472 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Please list the colleges, universities, or clubs where you competed in competitive athletics. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
