    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2739": {
      "title": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Administrative Assistant for the College of Business, Humanities, &amp; Technology",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Administrative Assistant for the College of Business, Humanities, &amp; Technology Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Administrative Assistant for the College of Business, Humanities, & Technology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Administrative Assistant for the College of Business, Humanities, & Technology Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division College of Business Department College of Business Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Under the direction of the Operations Manager for the College of Business, Humanities, & Technology, provide administrative support for the faculty and staff in the College in a fast-paced, collaborative environment. View full job description Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Hourly (Non-exempt) Salary Hourly: $16.79 - $17.66 Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a bachelor’s degree plus one year of experience in a collaborative office environment. Experience should demonstrate: Knowledge of basic office management systems and procedures Knowledge of MS Office products Knowledge of Google Workspace and project management software Ability to use typical office equipment Demonstrated interpersonal skills and customer service focus Accurate data entry and ability to transfer data from hard copy to digital databases Organizational skills and the ability to multitask Ability to set up Zoom or Google Meet video conferencing for meetings with Doane University divisions Preferred Qualifications Understanding of higher education processes Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Occasional weekend or evening work for campus events is expected. Travel Required No Physical Requirements Light work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF193 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2656 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
