    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2742": {
      "title": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Director of Marketing",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Director of Marketing Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Director of Marketing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Director of Marketing Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Enrollment Management Department Office of Strategic Marketing Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Doane University is looking for a Director of Marketing to provide transformative leadership to our marketing team. Reporting directly to the Vice President of Enrollment Management and Marketing, the successful candidate will have a critical eye for design and expertise in developing strategies to maximize the productivity of marketing spend. Responsibilities also include developing both short- and long-term strategic marketing initiatives that achieve the university’s goals and promote the mission, vision, values, and purpose. View full job description Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Salaried (Exempt) Salary Minimum Required Qualifications Requires a bachelor’s degree and five (5) or more years of experience that includes: Related strategic communications, marketing, and publications roles. Track record of developing and implementing strategic communications and marketing plans. Website management and user experience. Social media and multimedia engagement and campaigns. The successful applicant must demonstrate: A desire to represent Doane University. Ability to think strategically using a data-driven, results-based approach. Outstanding management, creative, and leadership abilities, and a proven capacity for collaboration. Superior verbal/non-verbal and written communication skills. Strong interpersonal and organizational skills A high energy level and willingness to take a hands-on approach to developing and executing communication activities that range from routine to highly creative. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Ability to influence constituents quickly and positively. Capable of creative, efficient, and effective problem-solving. Preferred Qualifications A master’s degree is preferred Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel Required No Physical Requirements Light work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF200 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2741 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Portfolio Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
