    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2747": {
      "title": "Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Financial Aid Counselor Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Financial Aid Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Position Details Position Information Position Title Financial Aid Counselor Job Type Full Time - 12 months Division Enrollment Management Department Financial Aid Office Job Location Crete, NE (68333) Position Summary Doane University , a liberal arts university in Crete, Nebraska, is hiring a Financial Aid Counselor to provide excellent customer service and guidance to students and their families. Don’t let a lack of financial aid experience stop you from applying! While a background in financial aid is a plus, it is not mandatory. Your desire to help others succeed and the ability to show respect for each person’s situation is far more important to us. We provide thorough training to ensure your success in providing assistance with all aspects of financial aid, including determining eligibility, clarifying policies, managing the loan processes, and providing information on financing options. View full job description Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the University. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. FLSA Hourly (Non-exempt) Salary $18.50 - $22.00 Minimum Required Qualifications Requires an associate’s degree and two (2) years of experience in a highly regulated field that includes managing deadlines, maintaining detailed, accurate records, and ensuring confidentiality and compliance; customer service experience that includes de-escalation and problem-solving; effective verbal and written communication with internal partners and external customers. Applicants must be able to demonstrate: Genuine desire to help others succeed Commitment to showing respect for each person’s situation. The ability to explain complex processes with confidence and empathy. A track record of follow-through and personal accountability. Preferred Qualifications A bachelor’s degree and experience with financial aid in higher education are preferred. Experience that demonstrates the following is a plus: Collaboration across departments or functional offices. Compliance with the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act ( FERPA ). Successful use of technology to determine student eligibility and originate a financial aid award. Able to explain, in lay terms, available types of financial aid, scholarships, and general student eligibility criteria. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with diverse families. Required Licenses/Certifications Preferred Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Occasional travel between Lincoln and Crete Campuses Travel Required No Physical Requirements Sedentary work Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Background Check Required Yes Posting Detail Information Posting Number STF201 Desired Start Date Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Doane offers a comprehensive benefits package that supports you professionally and personally, including paid time off, health and retirement benefits, professional development opportunities, and free undergraduate and discounted graduate tuition. Visit our benefits page to learn more. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2745 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Is the salary or salary range listed in the job posting acceptable to you? Yes No * Please describe any previous experience you have working in a customer service enviornment (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Document Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2709": {
      "title": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant or Associate Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Doane University Jobs and Careers | Assistant or Associate Professor of Finance Skip to Main Content Jobs and Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About Doane Lincoln Campus Omaha Location Assistant or Associate Professor of Finance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further inquiries on the position, please email Sara Simonsen, Operations Manager of the College of Business, Humanities, and Technology, sara.simonsen@doane.edu . Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcript of graduate degrees or graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Finance Unit College of Business Job Location Crete, NE & Lincoln, NE Description of Work The School of Business and Leadership ( SBL ) at Doane University is seeking applicants for a full-time tenure-track faculty position as an Assistant or Associate Professor of Finance. The SBL at Doane University is ACBSP -accredited and serves both undergraduate and graduate students at campuses located in Crete and Lincoln, Nebraska. The SBL provides a highly collaborative and collegial environment that is very supportive of teaching, scholarship activities, and faculty development. Responsibilities will include teaching a total of up to 24 credit hours per academic year across a variety of finance courses. Course modality could include both online and in-person sections. Course location could include both Crete residential campus and Lincoln non-residential campus, teaching both undergraduate and graduate students. We have a strong interest in faculty with expertise in one or more areas, including corporate finance, fintech, investments, financial planning, and business valuation. The anticipated start date for the position is August 2027. Doane University actively works to create and sustain a welcoming learning community for all members to fulfill their potential, feel valued, and make meaningful contributions to the university. Doane University is an equal-opportunity employer and seeks candidates who reflect the diversity of our society. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Doane University does not provide employment visa sponsorship for this position. Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. or DBA in Finance earned or in progress Academically qualified to meet ACBSP accreditation standards Successful experience as an instructor in finance Commitment to ongoing professional activity and scholarship Candidates must have knowledge of methods to effectively instruct, motivate, and evaluate both undergraduate and graduate students, as well as: Teach across a variety of modalities Engage in faculty scholarly and service activities Participate in continuous improvement efforts within the SBL Preferred Qualifications Relevant industry experience Undergraduate, graduate, face-to-face, and online teaching experience Required Licenses/Certifications Physical/Environmental/Working Conditions Working Conditions Travel between Doane campuses in Crete and Lincoln Travel Required Background Check Required Yes Outdoor Exposure Primarily exposed to indoor elements Posting Detail Information Posting Number FAC058 Desired Start Date 08/09/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Review Start Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For further inquiries on the position, please email Sara Simonsen, Operations Manager of the College of Business, Humanities, and Technology, sara.simonsen@doane.edu . Apply with a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and one (1) PDF of transcripts of all graduate work (unofficial accepted for applications). You will be asked for contact information for three references on the application form. Official transcript of graduate degrees or graduate degree in progress will be required as a condition of employment. Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://doane.peopleadmin.com/postings/2642 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Doane University 1014 Boswell Ave. Crete, NE 68333 Back to top © Doane University is an equal opportunity educator and employer. This site is produced and maintained by Doane University. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
